9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "clockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523367} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6e12f4-9d18-5592-b8ff-e4e7d21e2354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "counterclockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35c949f2-67bb-5cc5-ab89-4f36613e0369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "clockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523367} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0ed1170-20ac-57d4-8bc2-7e1c095e6a0c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523879} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5af3527-a165-5d7d-83fe-e90f66fd95dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a\\ne 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523669} {:answer/id #uuid "ce65b786-439c-5486-ad9e-d2dd2ab1cd2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523686} {:answer/id #uuid "debc4a56-1da5-5922-a8fd-52a2d630e6b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce65b786-439c-5486-ad9e-d2dd2ab1cd2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523686} :answer-field/id #uuid "f17043e1-9f96-5f60-95a4-3f465e8429cb" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef6edd26-9db3-5670-acfc-376735700ecd" :question/math-academy-id "q-334268" :question/problem "![](images/97/97291bd2f6b0a958a6651a87076a8ea313bec31cd6004840e0d81247dc364bf8.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two complex eigenvalues $\\lambda =a\\pm b\\text{i},$ where $a,b\\in R,$ is shown above. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe given curve is \n{{field-1}},\nrepresenting\n{{field-2}}\nthat is traversed \n{{field-3}}.\nThus, we must have \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that the given curve is $\\text{bounded}$ (and closed), representing $\\text{an ellipse}$ that is traversed $\\text{clockwise}.$\n\nBut we have that:\n\n- ${e}^{at}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty $ when $a>0,$ and\n\n- ${e}^{at}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty $ when $a<0.$\n\nThus, we must have $a=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166942 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b542bd66-f4f8-5b4e-a3e7-4717827c427a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parameters of a System Given Its Phase Portrait"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answ